---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';

import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro';

import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../../consts';
import Project from '../../components/Project.astro';

const title = `${SITE_TITLE}'s Projects`
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
		<style>
			[data-icon] {
				width: 48px;
				height: 48px;
				margin-right: 5px;
			}

			main {
				width: 960px;
			}

			main h3 span {
				text-shadow: 3px 3px 10px black;
			}

			ul {
				list-style-type: none;
			}

			li {
				margin-bottom: 48px;
			}

			li * {
				text-decoration: none;
				transition: 0.2s ease;
			}

			ul, li {
				margin-top: 0px;
			}

			ul li {
				text-decoration: none;
				transition: 0.2s ease;
			}

			ul li a {
				display: block;
			}

			h3 {
				margin-top: 1.5rem;
			}

			p {
				margin-top: 0px;
				line-height: 2rem;
			}

			#title {
				margin-bottom: 103px;
			}

			.links {
				display: flex;
				justify-content: flex-end;
			}

			.scribble {
				width: auto;
				height: 50px;
			}

			@media (max-width: 40rem) {
				.scribble {
					display: none;
				}
			}

            .project-img {
    			display: block;
    			margin-left: auto;
    			margin-right: auto;
				margin-bottom: 10px;
    			width: 100%;
    			height: 200px;
    			object-fit: cover;
    			overflow: hidden;
			}	

			.bottom-img {
				margin-left: 50rem;
			}

			.special-box {
				margin: 18px;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h3 id="title" class="center-text">⛏️ <span>Projects</span> ⛏️</h3>
			<div>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<Project 
							name="Character Sheets"
							src="/projects/CharacterSheets.png" 
							alt="A demo image of the minimal process to using the Character Sheets plugin"
							github="https://github.com/Grayvox/obsidian-character-sheets"
						>
							Have you ever wanted to streamline the creation of characters for a novel, TTRPG, game concept, 
							film, or any other form of storytelling? I sure have! And now I can satisfy my visions of 
							tormenting my characters with the power of Obsidian - using the Character Sheets plugin! Using
							this simple plugin, you can quickly generate a new character sheet with presets depending on
							your case, and customize it to your heart's content!	
						</Project>
					</li>
					<li>
						<Project 
							name="Dawg"
							src="/projects/Dawg.png" 
							alt="A demo image of Dawg in action"
							github="https://github.com/Grayvox/dawg"
						>
							Dawg is a lot of things that I can't seem to decide on - but the best way to say for now is that
							it's an easy to use Discord bot that allows me to streamline the process of managing my Discord
							server - from fancy embeds for my stream schedule, to commands to provide info on my current
							projects, Dawg has it all! ...And is being updated regularly when my brain comes up with something
							else to work on...
						</Project>
					</li>
					<li>
						<Project 
							name="They Are Unworthy"
							src="/projects/TheyAreUnworthy.png" 
							alt="They Are Unworthy logo"
							itch="https://grayvox.itch.io/they-are-unworthy"
						>
							You are the final say. The judge, if you will. The one who decides who on death row deserves life 
							or not. As designated by the Supervisors, you enter your room of judgement, read the reason that 
							the prisoner behind the window is on death row, and use the terminal before you to decide their fate. 
							Though not everything is as it seems… you know the Supervisors can be harsh, and that everyone has a 
							story.  But if you take too long, the Supervisors will take notice and make the decision before you 
							can...  and of course, lower your approval rating with it.
							<br>
							<br>
							Will you decide if they are worthy of living, or not?
							<br>
							<br>
							<i>Built for the 16th Pirate Software Game Jam, with help from GTortle and Perny</i>
						</Project>
					</li>
					<li>
						<Project 
							name="Noirdo"
							src="/projects/Noirdo.png" 
							alt="Noirdo logo"
							itch="https://grayvox.itch.io/noirdo"
						>
							In a dark, heavily guarded castle, specially trained alchemists known as Shadow Benders house hundreds 
							of shadow creatures known as noirdos in cages. The noirdos are used to make powerful potions to fight 
							in the coming war… but one Noirdo is determined to escape before he meets this fate.	
							<br>
							<br>
							<i>Built for the 15th Pirate Software Game Jam, with help from GTortle</i>
						</Project>
					</li>
					<li>
						<Project 
							name="Hangman"
							src="/projects/Hangman.png" 
							alt="A demo image of the minimal process to using the Character Sheets plugin"
							github="https://github.com/Grayvox/hangman"
						>
							A recreation of the word solving game, Hangman. Uses serialization to save and load game files 
							as the user wishes. Written in Ruby and for the command line.
						</Project>
					</li>
					<li>
						<Project 
							name="Mastermind"
							src="/projects/Mastermind.png" 
							alt="A demo image of the minimal process to using the Character Sheets plugin"
							github="https://github.com/Grayvox/mastermind"
						>
							A recreation of the code breaking game, Mastermind, written in Ruby and for the command line.
						</Project>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<img class="bottom-img" src="/scribbles/FoundTheEnd.png" alt="Welp, found the end. Congrats!">
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>